-- ERROR ---------------- errors/duplicate_binder_3.march

`a` is bound twice in the same parameter list or pattern. [duplicate_binder]

4 |   fn pick(0, a, a) : Int do a end
                    ^

    A parameter list or a pattern binds each name once, so there is no single value this name could refer to.
    Rename one of them, or write `_` for an argument you don't use. To require two values to be equal, bind two names and compare them in a `when` guard: `(a, a2) when a == a2 -> …`.

    first bound here:

4 |   fn pick(0, a, a) : Int do a end
                 ^
    run `march --explain duplicate_binder`


